BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 622.00 Td (Most cached tokens are rarely attended to. HARBOR is a training-free eviction policy that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 609.00 Td (keeps only a fixed budget of the key-value cache: the first tokens of the sequence, a window) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 596.00 Td (of recent tokens, and the heavy hitters that have received the most attention so far. At a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 583.00 Td (cache budget of 20% HARBOR keeps 97.8% of the full-cache accuracy on LongSuite.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 563.00 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 543.00 Td (Attention in trained language models is sparse: in a typical layer, five percent of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 530.00 Td (tokens receive more than half of the attention mass. If the tokens that matter can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 517.00 Td (identified while decoding, the rest of the cache can be dropped without retraining.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 497.00 Td (2 Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 477.00 Td (HARBOR always keeps the first four tokens because they act as attention sinks: the softmax) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 464.00 Td (must place its mass somewhere, and models learn to park it on the first positions, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 451.00 Td (evicting them changes every later attention distribution. It also keeps the 256 most recent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 438.00 Td (tokens, which carry the local context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 418.00 Td (The remaining budget goes to heavy hitters. Each cached token keeps a running sum of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 405.00 Td (attention it has received from all queries so far, and HARBOR ranks tokens by this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 392.00 Td (accumulated attention score. When the cache is full the token with the lowest score outside) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 72.00 379.00 Td (the sinks and the recent window is evicted.) Tj ET
